    ("argocd-multi-source", "Multiple Sources & App Composition", "gitops", "advanced", "Multi-source Applications combine manifests or values from several repositories. This can separate chart and configuration ownership, but increases provenance and version coordination requirements.", "Chart source + values-only Git source pinned to a commit"),
    ("argocd-private-repo", "Private Repositories & Credential Templates", "security", "intermediate", "Repository credentials grant repo-server access to source code. Use read-only deploy keys or scoped tokens, prefer credential templates and rotate credentials without exposing them to app teams.", "Repository secret with url prefix and narrowly scoped token"),
    ("argocd-sync", "Manual Sync, Automated Sync & Retry", "sync", "basic", "Manual sync applies a reviewed revision; automated sync reconciles eligible differences according to policy. Retry behavior handles transient failures but should not mask invalid manifests or policy errors.", "argocd app sync payments-prod"),
    ("argocd-prune", "Prune & Deletion Semantics", "sync", "intermediate", "Prune removes live resources absent from desired state. Enable deliberately, understand propagation and finalizers, and protect stateful or externally managed resources from accidental deletion.", "Automated sync with prune enabled after reviewing diff"),
    ("argocd-self-heal", "Self Heal & Live Drift Correction", "sync", "intermediate", "Self-heal reverts live drift toward Git. It is useful for owned declarative resources but can fight autoscalers, operators and other controllers unless ownership is modeled correctly.", "Enable selfHeal only on fields Argo CD owns"),
    ("argocd-sync-waves", "Sync Waves & Resource Ordering", "sync", "intermediate", "Sync waves order resources by annotation; negative waves run earlier and health gates progress between phases. Avoid treating wave order as a substitute for readiness or dependency design.", "argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: \"-1\""),
    ("argocd-hooks", "PreSync, Sync & PostSync Hooks", "sync", "advanced", "Hooks run Jobs or other resources around sync phases for migrations and verification. Define delete policy, idempotence, timeout and failure recovery for hooks that may be retried.", "argocd.argoproj.io/hook: PreSync"),
    ("argocd-health", "Health Assessment & Custom Health Checks", "sync", "intermediate", "Argo CD health status reflects resource readiness; custom health checks can describe CRD-specific status. Health must align with application readiness and avoid reporting healthy before user traffic is safe.", "Check Deployment availableReplicas and custom resource status.conditions"),
    ("argocd-sync-options", "Sync Options: Apply, Replace & Server-Side Apply", "sync", "advanced", "Sync options alter Kubernetes apply behavior, field ownership, replacement and pruning. Choose per resource based on object size, ownership and API semantics; review destructive effects first.", "ServerSideApply=true on a resource with managed field ownership"),
    ("argocd-diff-options", "Diff Customization & Ignore Differences", "operations", "intermediate", "Diff customization ignores known controller-managed fields or normalizes representations. Narrow ignore rules to exact JSON pointers or managers so meaningful drift remains visible.", "Ignore /spec/replicas when HPA exclusively owns the field"),
    ("argocd-sync-windows", "Sync Windows & Change Calendars", "sync", "intermediate", "Sync windows allow or deny automated sync during defined schedules and can include manual override policy. Time zones and application targeting should be explicit and tested.", "Deny production sync during freeze; permit approved manual override"),
    ("argocd-rollback", "Rollback, Git Revert & Desired State", "sync", "intermediate", "Git revert is the durable rollback path for GitOps because it restores desired state. Argo CD rollback can temporarily apply a prior revision; reconcile Git afterward to prevent reversion.", "Revert deployment commit → Argo CD syncs previous image digest"),
    ("argocd-app-project", "AppProjects: Repository & Destination Guardrails", "security", "intermediate", "AppProjects constrain source repositories, target destinations and resource kinds. Separate team projects and deny cluster-scoped resources unless ownership requires them.", "sourceRepos allow list + destinations namespace allow list"),
    ("argocd-rbac", "Argo CD RBAC Policies & SSO Groups", "security", "advanced", "RBAC maps authenticated users/groups to actions on applications, projects and repositories. Use SSO groups, least privilege and explicit deny for high-risk operations.", "team-payments may sync payments-prod but cannot edit project policy"),
    ("argocd-sso", "SSO, OIDC & Local Accounts", "security", "intermediate", "OIDC integration centralizes authentication and group claims. Disable or tightly restrict local accounts and verify claim mapping and token lifetime.", "Map IdP `groups` claim to Argo CD RBAC roles"),
    ("argocd-cluster-credentials", "Register Clusters & Credential Boundaries", "security", "advanced", "Argo CD cluster credentials determine where the controller can deploy. Use dedicated service accounts, namespace scope where possible and separate control planes for distinct trust boundaries.", "Register cluster with deploy role limited to approved namespaces"),
    ("argocd-secret-management", "Secrets in GitOps: SOPS & External Secrets", "security", "advanced", "GitOps needs encrypted or external secret workflows; plain Kubernetes Secret manifests expose base64 data in Git. Control decryption keys and keep secret rendering out of logs.", "SOPS-encrypted values decrypted by a scoped repo-server plugin or controller"),
    ("argocd-project-role", "Project Roles & Application Permissions", "security", "intermediate", "Project roles grant scoped actions and can issue tokens for automation. Keep token expiration and revocation documented and avoid broad project-admin roles for deployment bots.", "Project role deployer: get, sync applications in project only"),
    ("argocd-appset-model", "ApplicationSet Controllers & Templates", "scale", "basic", "ApplicationSets generate many Applications from cluster, Git, list, matrix or pull-request generators. Treat generated app names, project assignment and destination templating as security-critical.", "ApplicationSet generator → one Application per approved cluster/environment"),
    ("argocd-cluster-generator", "Cluster Generator & Fleet Deployments", "scale", "intermediate", "The cluster generator uses registered cluster labels to produce Applications. Labels select fleet membership and should be controlled to prevent an unauthorized cluster receiving production workloads.", "Match cluster label env=prod and region=us-east-1"),
    ("argocd-git-generator", "Git Directory & File Generators", "scale", "intermediate", "Git generators discover app directories or config files and template one Application per entry. Validate paths and metadata and avoid broad untrusted branch discovery for production.", "directories: path: services/*"),
    ("argocd-matrix-generator", "Matrix & Merge Generators", "scale", "advanced", "Matrix combines generator outputs into a product; merge overlays matching parameter sets. Control expansion size and ensure all combinations produce unique, authorized destinations.", "Matrix: clusters × service directories with bounded labels"),
    ("argocd-pull-request-generator", "Preview Environments with Pull Request Generator", "scale", "advanced", "PR generators create ephemeral apps for open changes. Restrict source repositories, namespaces, credentials, network access and cleanup of closed or stale previews.", "PR #42 → payments-pr-42 namespace → auto-delete on close"),
    ("argocd-appset-progressive", "Progressive Rollouts & Fleet Waves", "scale", "advanced", "Fleet rollout sequencing can partition clusters by labels or use progressive delivery controllers. Define health gates, pause conditions and rollback behavior for partial deployment.", "Canary cluster group → verify SLO → regional wave → full fleet"),
    ("argocd-appset-debug", "Debug Missing or Duplicate Generated Apps", "scale", "intermediate", "Generated Applications depend on generator inputs, templates, naming and controller logs. Inspect generator preview, labels, path filters and destination parameters before editing live Applications.", "argocd appset list; inspect generated parameters and controller events"),
    ("argocd-outofsync", "Diagnose OutOfSync State", "operations", "basic", "OutOfSync means rendered desired state differs from live state after normalization. Inspect resource-level diff and identify ownership, defaulting, mutation or stale source revision before syncing.", "argocd app diff payments-prod"),
    ("argocd-degraded", "Diagnose Degraded & Progressing Applications", "operations", "intermediate", "Application health aggregates resource status. Find the first unhealthy workload and inspect events, probes, image pulls, dependencies and custom health checks rather than repeatedly syncing.", "kubectl describe deployment and pods in the target namespace"),
    ("argocd-repo-server", "Repo Server Rendering & Plugin Failures", "operations", "advanced", "Repo-server fetches sources and renders manifests; dependency downloads, plugins, memory and credentials can cause comparison failures. Keep plugins pinned, isolated and constrained.", "Check repo-server logs, manifest generation error, tool versions and repository access"),
    ("argocd-large-apps", "Large Applications, Sharding & Controller Scale", "operations", "advanced", "Large apps and many clusters increase cache, diff and reconciliation load. Partition ownership, tune controller sharding and resource limits, and monitor queue and repo-server latency.", "Split unrelated services into Applications; shard controller by cluster"),
    ("argocd-webhooks", "Git Webhooks, Polling & Refresh", "operations", "intermediate", "Webhooks trigger prompt refresh while polling remains a fallback. Verify webhook secret, endpoint delivery and event filters; excessive force-refresh can add load.", "POST repository webhook → refresh only changed Application paths"),
    ("argocd-cli", "Argo CD CLI: app get, diff, sync & wait", "operations", "basic", "The CLI inspects app state, diffs manifests, syncs and waits for health. Pin context/server and namespace to avoid issuing a valid command against the wrong cluster.", "argocd app get payments-prod && argocd app diff payments-prod"),
    ("argocd-audit", "Audit Sync Identity & Change History", "operations", "intermediate", "Argo CD history links syncs to revisions and users, while Kubernetes audit logs show API actions. Correlate revision, actor, app and destination during incident review.", "argocd app history payments-prod"),
    ("argocd-notifications", "Notifications & Change Events", "operations", "intermediate", "Notifications can report sync, health and deployment events to chat or incident systems. Include revision, destination and safe links; avoid duplicating every reconciliation event.", "Notify on failed sync and healthy production deployment with revision URL"),
    ("argocd-resource-exclusions", "Resource Inclusions, Exclusions & Discovery", "operations", "advanced", "Resource discovery settings affect which API kinds Argo CD tracks and reconciles. Exclusions can hide drift, so scope and document them and verify cluster-scoped resource ownership.", "Exclude only a known externally managed kind with explicit ownership"),
    ("argocd-finalizers", "Finalizers, Cascading Deletes & App Deletion", "operations", "advanced", "Application finalizers control cascading resource deletion. App deletion can remove managed resources; protect production apps, understand orphan behavior and require deliberate authorization.", "Review finalizer and deletion propagation before removing an Application"),
    ("argocd-resource-tracking", "Resource Tracking & Shared Ownership", "operations", "advanced", "Argo CD tracks resources with labels, annotations or configured methods. Shared ownership or duplicate Applications can cause conflicting sync and prune decisions.", "Assign each Kubernetes object to one authoritative Application"),
    ("argocd-hooks-cleanup", "Hook Cleanup, TTL & Stuck Jobs", "operations", "intermediate", "Hook resources need delete policies or TTL cleanup; failed Jobs can block later syncs. Inspect hook phase, finalizers and status before manually removing resources.", "Hook delete policy: BeforeHookCreation,HookSucceeded"),
    ("argocd-upgrades", "Upgrade Argo CD & CRD Compatibility", "operations", "advanced", "Argo CD upgrades change controller, CRDs and API behavior. Read upgrade notes, back up configuration, test plugins and custom health scripts, and roll out control-plane changes separately from app changes.", "Upgrade staging control plane → verify sync and RBAC → promote version"),
    ("argocd-disaster-recovery", "Argo CD Disaster Recovery & Bootstrap", "operations", "advanced", "Git should contain enough configuration to recreate Applications and projects, while cluster credentials and secrets need protected recovery. Test bootstrap from a clean control plane.", "Install control plane → restore repo credentials securely → sync bootstrap apps"),
    ("argocd-application-health", "Custom Health for Operators & CRDs", "sync", "advanced", "Custom health Lua or built-in assessments interpret CRD status. Health checks should reflect readiness conditions and avoid treating an empty status as healthy.", "Mark custom resource healthy only when Ready=True and observedGeneration matches"),
    ("argocd-sync-failures", "Sync Failure: Apply, Admission & Webhooks", "operations", "intermediate", "Apply failures can come from invalid manifests, RBAC, quotas, admission policies or unavailable APIs. Use app events and Kubernetes events to find the rejecting layer and exact object.", "argocd app sync --dry-run; inspect admission error and resource event"),
    ("argocd-field-ownership", "Server-Side Apply & Field Manager Conflicts", "operations", "advanced", "Server-side apply tracks field managers and can surface conflicts with operators or humans. Decide which controller owns each field and avoid force-conflicts without reviewing data loss.", "Inspect managedFields before enabling ServerSideApply or force"),
    ("argocd-app-of-apps", "App of Apps Bootstrap Pattern", "gitops", "intermediate", "An app-of-apps manages child Application manifests from Git for bootstrap. Restrict its project and source because it can indirectly create broad deployment authority.", "Bootstrap app in platform project creates team Applications from allow-listed paths"),
    ("argocd-git-branch-policy", "Revision Pinning & Production Branch Policy", "security", "intermediate", "Production sources should use protected branches, tags or commit SHAs with review requirements. Mutable branch references need audit and branch protection to prevent unreviewed deployment.", "Require signed, approved commits to the prod configuration branch"),
    ("argocd-image-updater", "Image Updates & Git Write-Back", "gitops", "advanced", "Image Updater or automation can discover new tags and write updated values back to Git. Prefer digest pinning and pull requests so image selection remains reviewable and auditable.", "Update image digest in config repo branch and open a promotion PR"),
